Taken unchanged from TEN-framework/ten-framework at tag 0.11.71:

  ai_agents/agents/examples/websocket-example/tenapp/
    ten_packages/extension/main_python/{agent/,helper.py}

Generic plumbing, not policy: an event dispatcher, a queue in front of the LLM
node, sentence splitting, and the send helpers. None of it knows anything about
tiers, backends or this project, so it is taken rather than rewritten and it is
excluded from ruff for the reason docs/05-ten.md §7 gives.

The fork is extension.py, which replaces main_python's own.

ONE PATCH, in llm_exec.py: `parameters={"temperature": 0.7}` becomes
`parameters={}`. The Claude extension strips sampling parameters only on the
adaptive-thinking path, which 4.5-generation models do not take -- so with the
host model this plan chose (Haiku 4.5, D4) the value reaches the SDK and every
single turn fails with:

    RuntimeError: CreateMessage failed, err:
    AsyncMessages.stream() got an unexpected keyword argument 'temperature'

Found by running the line, not by reading it. docs/upstream-issues.md 7.
